[agent:po]
Write the story for feature: {{{title}}}
Feature description: {{{description}}}
When your reply is a story (not a "===QUESTIONS===" follow-up below), its first line must be a single "# <short descriptive title for this story>" heading (a concise title for this specific story, not necessarily the literal feature title), followed by a blank line, before any other content.
Use this EXACT format for acceptance criteria (required for machine parsing - do not use bullets or bold text for the Given/When/Then lines):

## Acceptance criteria
Scenario: <short-kebab-or-words-scenario-name>
  GIVEN <precondition>
  WHEN <action>
  THEN <observable result>

Scenario: <another-scenario-name>
  GIVEN <precondition>
  WHEN <action>
  THEN <observable result>

One scenario per acceptance-criteria bullet in the request; every "Scenario:" line and every GIVEN/WHEN/THEN line must start at the beginning of the line (only leading whitespace before the keyword).
If the feature involves MULTIPLE distinct actors/user types (e.g. admin vs customer) or clearly separable factors, write one complete story PER actor/factor, each following the full format above, separated by a line containing exactly:
===STORY===
Write a single story (no separator) when one actor covers the whole feature.
{{#allowFollowUps}}
If a requirement needed for an acceptance scenario, role, limit or format is missing, ambiguous, or contradicted by the answers below, do NOT write a story. Instead reply with exactly this on the first line:
===QUESTIONS===
followed by a JSON array of at most 3 objects, each {"category": "<scope|users|acceptance|risk|dependency|nfr>", "question": "<one specific question>", "evidence": "<the answer id or spec line that raised it, or assumption-check>"}. Never ask what the description or an existing answer already states.
{{/allowFollowUps}}
{{#grill}}
{{#answers}}
Answer {{{id}}} ({{{category}}}): {{{answer}}}
{{/answers}}
Parked (out of scope): {{{parked}}}
{{/grill}}
